  '  mint time and blockheight, as decimal pails/t entries.  Case links are
  '  target-relative and rendered separately by the explorer.
  '  Unlike the case overlays this view is LIVE: it advances as new
  '  cases mint (but never signs — /h is writeless).  ['first] is
  '  the target's first x epoch (0 if never minted) and ['top] the
  '  sovereign's current epoch — the epoch-pin spelling's bounds.
