  '  Time travel: /h/care/case/len/...path resolves (care, case)
  '  against the first len path segments via the sov's historical
  '  queries and dips the remainder into the answer.  Structural
  '  levels above the target carry non-enumerating markers because a
  '  local case has no meaning until the target is complete.
  '  Committed-only, and constant: nothing is ever
  '  written under /h, so a given /h path's answer never changes once
  '  known — subscriptions here are throwaway.
  \  pax=path s=sov
  ^  axal[myth]
  =  > none (axal/new[myth] .none)
  =  > n pax.len
  ?  (lt n 2)
     =  > a0 (axal/new[myth] (./some (h_mark "time travel: /h/care/case/len/...path resolves (care, case) against the first len segments of the path and dips the rest into the answer. x is the record, y adds the nearest-live frontier, z the whole subtree. an e<epoch> case segment pins the shared sovereign epoch instead of a target-local case. /h/v/len/...path is the version view. read only.")))
