  ^  maybe[iota]
  =  > es diffs.tap
  |  > i=nat 0
  ^  maybe[iota]
  ?  (ge i es.len)
     .none
  =  [p q]  es.at(i)
  =  > wrote=myth
       ?  q
        > (./make t=myth)  t
        > (./poke t=myth)  t
        > .cull  myth/new
  ?  ?=(.cull q)
     (_ i.inc)
  =  > cur=myth
       ?  s.x_latest(p)
        > (./known t=myth)  t
        > .null  myth/new
        > .unknown  myth/new
  =  > adopt
       '  the write CHANGES the contract: dispatched talks carry
       '  the whole melded record, so mere presence is not adoption
       ?  wrote.get(['sys 'lash])
        > .none  .false
        > (./some nl=pail)
          ?  cur.get(['sys 'lash])
           > .none  .true
           > (./some ol=pail)  !(equal nl ol)
  ?  adopt
     (_ i.inc)
  =  > final=myth
       ?  ?=((./make _) q)
          wrote
       (myth/meld wrote cur)
  ?  (fit_check final)
   > .none  (_ i.inc)
   > (./some why=iota)  (./some why)
+  commit
  '  Apply a fate to the sovereign: writs become raw step diffs.  The
  '  namespace expands recursive culls, rejects live writes through
  '  unrevived tombstones, then melds and deduplicates resolved values.
  '  Shape contracts gate here too: a diff whose final record carries
  '  ['sys 'lash] must fit it (/guard_diffs) or the event rejects.
  '  The accepted event owns one internal epoch; every affected
  '  (path, care) mints at most one independent local case.  Apollo
  '  time and PKI blockheight are zeroed in this port — the runtime
  '  supplies them a layer out.
  '  When journal is set, a /log/<epoch> node carrying the driving
  '  task, its ack, and its effects rides the same diff set — the
  '  event and its journal entry are one epoch, indivisible.
